revision.text:
[[File:Captain's log sea charting interface.png|thumb|right|The [[Captain's log]] displaying some sea charting tasks for the Port of Sarim.]]
[[File:Sea charting icon.png|left]]
'''Sea charting''' is a [[Sailing]] activity in which players perform tasks around the sea to receive one-time rewards of experience and items. The [[Captain's log]] contains records of completed charting tasks and hints for where to find incomplete ones. These tasks vary from simple exploration to puzzles and even data collection, many of which require specific tools to complete.

Charting tools can be collected from your ship's cargo hold or from the associated task NPC. The [[crowbar]] is rewarded upon completion of the quest [[Prying Times]], and the [[current duck]] is rewarded upon completion of [[Current Affairs]].

Completing every charting task requires 78 Sailing{{Boostable|yes}} or higher, as well as an [[eternal brazier]] to navigate through [[icy seas]] and a [[adamant helm]] or better to navigate through [[tangled kelp]] and [[crystal-flecked waters]].

For all experience rewards from charting, categorised into lists of seas and tasks, see [[Sea charting/By oceans|this page]].

Upon completing all charting tasks for a location, [[rapids]] will appear. Players with the appropriate [[helm]] built on their boat can gain a small speed boost by navigating through these rapids.

==Tools==
Charting tools are used to complete various charting tasks. Each type of task grants a certain amount of [[Sailing]] experience upon completion, and the required levels for these activities can be [[temporary skill boost|boosted]].
[[File:Spyglass location bubbles.png|thumb|right|A location where the [[spyglass]] can be used.]]
[[File:Current duck location ripples.png|thumb|right|A location where the [[current duck]] can be used.]]

The below charting tools can be withdrawn from the [[cargo hold]] interface on a [[boat]], as long as the tools are not already kept in the [[inventory]] or the [[bank]]. Charting tools that are lost or destroyed can always be retrieved from this cargo hold. Players can withdraw these tools separately or right-click to "Take all".

