==Additional rewards==
Aside from various amounts of experience for doing tasks and completing seas and oceans, players unlock access to [[Rapids|rapid]] shortcuts with the completion of certain seas. To learn more about the experience earned from charting, head over to [[Sea charting/By oceans|this page]].

===Alcohol===
After completely charting certain amounts of [[sea|seas]], players can speak to [[Chartin'_Charles_McAtless|Charles]] in [[Pandemonium Cave]] for alcoholic beverages with temporary effects when consumed. These can also be stored in a [[Keg (facility)|keg]] on a [[player-owned ship]] for different longer-lasting benefits. Players require certain [[Sailing]] levels to be able to meet these requirements.

{|class="wikitable lighttable"
! colspan="2"|Alcohol || Level || Requirements || Temporary effects || [[Keg (facility)|Keg]] benefits
|-
|{{Plinkt|Kraken ink stout}} || {{SCP|Sailing|38}} || Completely chart 5 seas in the [[Ardent Ocean]], and 5 seas in the [[Unquiet Ocean]] ||
*+1 [[Sailing]]
*+2 [[Magic]]
|Increases the likelihood of [[ocean encounters]] by 4%
|-
|{{Plinkt|Perildance bitter}} || {{SCP|Sailing|38}} || Completely chart 8 seas in the [[Western Ocean]], and 5 seas in the [[Shrouded Ocean]] ||
*+1 [[Sailing]]
*+2 [[Ranged]] and [[Strength]]
*-2 [[Magic]]
|Increases the max hit of [[Cannon (Sailing)|cannons]] by one
|-
|{{Plinkt|Trawler's trust}} || {{SCP|Sailing|51}} || Completely chart 50 seas across all oceans ||
*+2 [[Sailing]] and [[Fishing]]
|Grants a 5% chance to catch an extra fish while [[deep sea trawling]]
|-
|{{Plinkt|Horizon's lure}} || {{SCP|Sailing|78}} || Completely chart 70 seas across all oceans ||
*+4 [[Sailing]]
*-2 [[Thieving]]
|Increases all Sailing experience gained by 2.5%
|}

===Boat paint===
After completely charting certain oceans, players can speak to [[Gerardus]] in [[Port Roberts]] with the [[Captain's log]] in their inventory to acquire certain items used to retrieve [[Boat paint]].

{|class="wikitable lighttable"
! colspan="2"|Boat paint || Level || Requirements
|-
|{{Plinkt|Saradominist paint}} || {{SCP|Sailing|38}} || Fully chart the [[Ardent Ocean]] to get the [[holy sheet]] from [[Gerardus]]. Then give the sheet to [[High Priest (Entrana)|High Priest]] on [[Entrana]].
|-
|{{Plinkt|Zamorakian paint}} || {{SCP|Sailing|60}} || Fully chart the [[Unquiet Ocean]] to get the [[charred key]] from [[Gerardus]]. Then use the key to open the [[old chest]] on [[Charred Island]].
|-
|{{Plinkt|Guthixian paint}} || {{SCP|Sailing|72}} || Fully chart the [[Shrouded Ocean]] to get the [[void orb]] from [[Gerardus]]. Then give the orb to the [[Elite Void Knight]].
|-
|{{Plinkt|Armadylean paint}} || {{SCP|Sailing|78}} || Fully chart the [[Northern Ocean]] to get the [[book about lighthouses]] from [[Gerardus]]. Then talk to [[Larrissa]] with the book.
''<small>Note: This requires completion of [[Horror from the Deep]].</small>''
|-
|}

===Experience===
Chartin' Charles also provides training that gives experience rewards upon completing entire oceans.  To claim bonus XP, the player must have their Captain's log in their inventory. Except for [[Mooring point|Mooring Points]], all of the requirements below are [[Temporary skill boost|boostable]], but at each charting instance the level requirement needs to be met. Therefore, realistically, boosting can be done using [[Beer glass|Beer Glasses]]  on the [[Keg (facility)|Keg facility]] loaded with [[Whirlpool surprise]], for a consistent +3 Sailing level boost. To receive the experience from Chartin' Charles the maximum level requirement for the specific ocean must also be met.

