{{Otheruses|cooked sea turtle|the raw form|Raw sea turtle}} {{External|rs|rsc}} {{Infobox Item |name = Sea turtle |image = [[File:Sea turtle.png]] |release = [[28 July]] [[2003]] |update = Trawler mini game |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |edible = Yes |options = Eat, Drop |examine = Tasty! |value = 200 |weight = 0.350 |exchange = Yes |id = 397 }} [[File:Sea turtle detail.png|left|180px]] '''Sea turtles''' are a type of [[food]] that restores 21 [[Hitpoints]] when eaten. It can be obtained by cooking [[raw sea turtle]] on a [[fire]] or [[cooking range]], requiring level 82 [[Cooking]] and granting 211.3 [[experience]] when successful. When cooking there is a chance to fail, resulting in a [[burnt sea turtle]]. The [[burn rate]] decreases as the player's Cooking level increases. Sea turtles never stop burning altogether even at level 99, unless the player is wearing a [[Cooking cape]].
Players without the [[cooking cape]] are encouraged to cook sea turtles on the clay oven within the [[Hosidius Kitchen]], as this provides the player the best chances to successfully cook them.
