{{Multi Infobox |text1 = Grown |item1 = {{Infobox Scenery |version1 = 3 plants |version2 = 2 plants |version3 = 1 plant |name = Seaweed |image1 = [[File:Seaweed (3 plants).png|x300px]] |image2 = [[File:Seaweed (2 plants).png|x300px]] |image3 = [[File:Seaweed (1 plant).png|x300px]] |release = [[7 September]] [[2017]] |update = Fossil Island |members = Yes |quest = No |location = [[Seaweed patch]] |options = Pick, Inspect, Guide |examine = A patch of seaweed. |map = No |id1 = 30491 |id2 = 30492 |id3 = 30493 |leagueRegion = Misthalin }} |text2 = Growing |item2 = {{Infobox Scenery |version1 = Stage 1 |version2 = Stage 2 |version3 = Stage 3 |version4 = Stage 4 |name = Seaweed |image1 = [[File:Seaweed (stage 1).png|x300px]] |image2 = [[File:Seaweed (stage 2).png|x300px]] |image3 = [[File:Seaweed (stage 3).png|x300px]] |image4 = [[File:Seaweed (stage 4).png|x300px]] |release = [[7 September]] [[2017]] |update = Fossil Island |members = Yes |quest = No |location = [[Seaweed patch]] |options = Inspect, Guide |examine1 = Seaweed spores have been sown in this farming patch. |examine2 = Seaweed is growing in this farming patch. |examine3 = Seaweed is growing in this farming patch. |examine4 = Seaweed is growing in this farming patch. |map = No |id1 = 30487 |id2 = 30488 |id3 = 30489 |id4 = 30490 |leagueRegion = Misthalin }} |text3 = Diseased |item3 = {{Infobox Scenery |version1 = Diseased, stage 2 |version2 = Diseased, stage 3 |version3 = Diseased, stage 4 |name = Diseased seaweed |image1 = [[File:Diseased seaweed (stage 2).png|x300px]] |image2 = [[File:Diseased seaweed (stage 3).png|x300px]] |image3 = [[File:Diseased seaweed (stage 4).png|x300px]] |release = [[7 September]] [[2017]] |update = Fossil Island |members = Yes |quest = No |location = [[Seaweed patch]] |options = Cure, Inspect, Guide |examine = This seaweed has become diseased. |map = No |id1 = 30494 |id2 = 30495 |id3 = 30496 |leagueRegion = Misthalin }} |text4 = Dead |item4 = {{Infobox Scenery |version1 = Dead, stage 2 |version2 = Dead, stage 3 |version3 = Dead, stage 4 |name = Dead seaweed |image1 = [[File:Dead seaweed (stage 2).png|x300px]] |image2 = [[File:Dead seaweed (stage 3).png|x300px]] |image3 = [[File:Dead seaweed (stage 4).png|x300px]] |release = [[7 September]] [[2017]] |update = Fossil Island |members = Yes |quest = No |location = [[Seaweed patch]] |options = Clear, Inspect, Guide |examine = This seaweed has become diseased and died. |map = No |id1 = 30497 |id2 = 30498 |id3 = 30499 |leagueRegion = Misthalin }} }} '''Seaweed''' is a [[Farming]] plant grown at level 23 Farming. Seaweed is grown by planting a [[seaweed spore]] in the [[seaweed patch]] in the [[underwater]] area of [[Fossil Island]]. Players can pay [[Mernia]] to protect this patch by giving her 200 [[numulite]]s.
Once fully grown, which takes approximately 40 minutes, players will be able to harvest [[giant seaweed]]. A minimum of three can be collected per patch, with the average being around 15–30 (if [[Supercompost|super]] or [[ultracompost]] is used; 8-16 if compost is not used), depending on one's Farming level. Specifically, the patch has three "lives" by default, and each tier of compost adds one extra. The chance to not consume a life upon harvest is 64.1% at level 23 and 82% at level 99, using linear interpolation for other levels.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1050735300119617536|date=12 October 2018|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/98771|archivedate=28 May 2020|quote=3 [lives] as standard. Add 1-3 for the tier of compost you used. The chance scales from 59% - 82% of NOT taking a life when you get an item, as your level goes from 1-99.}} When using ultracompost, there is a ~5% chance of disease per growth stage totaling ~18.5% over all 4 growth stages.
[[Magic secateurs]] and the [[farming cape]] '''do not''' have an effect.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1011197294019072000|date=25 June 2018|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/106736|archivedate=29 May 2020|quote=No, doesn't look like it. I guess you weren't expected to have them equipped down there.}} Having an [[attas plant]] growing in one's [[Farming Guild#Anima patch|anima patch]] will increase the yield of a seaweed patch however.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1164089277514440704|date=21 August 2019|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/102612|archivedate=30 April 2023|quote=[Just out of curiosity! Does the Attas Anima Plant affect Giant Seaweed yield?] Yes.}}
==Farming info== {{Farming info |name = Seaweed |level = 23 |patch = [[Seaweed patch|Seaweed]] |seed = {{plink|Seaweed spore}} |seedsper = 1 |payment = 200 {{plink|Numulite}}s |time = 40 min (4x10 min) |plant = [[Seaweed (Farming)|Seaweed]] |crop = {{plink|Giant seaweed}} |yield = 3+ ([[Variable crop yield|varies]]) |regrow = No |plantxp = 19 |checkxp = No |harvestxp = 21 }}
{{DropsTableHead}} {{DropsLineSkill|name=Giant seaweed|quantity=1|rarity=Always|skill=Farming}} {{DropsTableBottom}} {{reflist|group=d}}
===Average harvest yield=== Giant seaweed has a minimum of 3 [[Farming#Variable crop yield|harvest lives]], increasing by 1 for each tier of [[compost]] used (for a maximum of 6 when using [[ultracompost]]). While harvesting giant seaweed, there is a chance to not consume a harvest life dependent on the player's Farming level. This chance scales from 59.0% at level 1 to 82.4% at level 99, interpolating linearly in between.
