The '''Secluded Chapel''' is an old ruin found outside [[Shayzien]], south of the [[Giant Pit]]. 

Inside the chapel spawn 1 [[Coins|coin]], 1 [[Iron nails|iron nail]], and an [[Old note (Secluded Chapel)|old note]]. The altar slab '''cannot''' be used to restore [[Prayer points]]. There is a small graveyard, and the [[grave digger]] can be found just to the west.

{{Great Kourend}}
{{Places of worship}}

{{External|rs|dw}}
The '''Second Age''' is the period following the [[First Age]]. It is also the 'Golden Age' of [[Zaros]] and the [[Zarosian Empire]], until he was betrayed by [[Zamorak]]. This age approximately began when [[Guthix]] disappeared and descended deep beneath the earth, and is estimated to have been about 2,000 years long.

Numerous other [[god]]s began setting foot on [[Gielinor]]; [[Tumeken]], [[Elidinis]], [[Zaros]], [[Saradomin]], [[Armadyl]] and [[Bandos]] are known to have arrived during the Second Age, bringing with them new [[races]] to the world, gathering new followers and claiming territory.

==Major events==
*[[Tumeken]] and [[Elidinis]] both arrive on Gielinor, they supposedly meet by the [[River Elid]], fall in love, marry, and start a family, with Elidinis giving birth to their son and daughter; [[Icthlarin]] and [[Amascut]].{{CiteNPC|npc=Sphinx|quote= Icthlarin is the god of the dead. He is the son of Tumeken and Elidinis, and brother to the Devourer.}}
*[[Zaros]] arrives on Gielinor and together with his [[demon|demonic]] and [[vampyre|vampyric]]{{CiteText|text=Arachnids of vampyrium|author=|quote=When the Stranger from Afar led the vampyres to Gielinor...|page=|loc=Theatre of Blood|notes=Stranger from Afar refers to Zaros.|name=}}{{CiteText|text=The wild hunt|author=Lowerniel Drakan|quote=Before the Stranger from Afar domesticated us...|page=|loc=Theatre of Blood|notes=|name=}} followers, he establishes a vast [[Zarosian Empire|empire]].{{CiteNPC|npc=Eblis|quote=My ancestors lived far to the North of here, and our lands stretched from the sea in the East to the river Lum, and the mountain of ice. From coast to coast, North to South, our domain was absolute.|loc=Desert Treasure I|notes=|name=}}
*[[Saradomin]] arrives on Gielinor, specifically on the island of [[Entrana]]{{CiteNPC|npc=High Priest (Entrana)|quote=You are standing on the holy island of Entrana. It was here that Saradomin first stepped upon Gielinor. In homage to Saradomin's first arrival, we have built a great church, and devoted the island to those who wish peace for the world.|loc=Heroes' Quest|notes=Only during the Heroes' Quest}}, bringing with him the [[icyene]] and [[centaur]]s.
*[[Armadyl]] arrives on Gielinor, bringing with him his [[aviansie (race)|aviansie]].{{CitePostbag|letter=Letter 1|issue=15|author=[[Armacus]]|notes=Armacus is a [[Guardian of Armadyl]] and describes how Armadyl's army contained [[aviansie (race)|aviansie)]].}}{{CiteNPC|npc=Kree'arra|notes=Kree'arra is Armadyl's general during the God Wars, therefor Armadyl must have arrived in the 2nd age; before the God Wars.}}
*Tumeken creates the four minor [[Menaphite Pantheon|Menaphite deities]]; [[Apmeken]], [[Crondis]], [[Het]], and [[Scabaras]].{{CiteNPC|npc=High Priest (Sophanem)|loc=Contact!|quote=The Book of Light and Day says that Tumeken once fell into a deep sleep and dreamt for four days and four nights. The first night he slept and dreamt a good dream. He dreamt of a journey long and arduous. From the loins of his subconscious Apmeken was born into reality; a physical manifestation of his dream. Tumeken continued to have pleasant dreams for a further two days and two nights. After each, a new deity came into being. On the fourth night, however, Tumeken dreamt a bad dream. He dreamt of himself and he dreamt of his increasing isolation caused by his extended sleep. This isolation sprung forth into the world and took the form of Scabaras.}}
*The [[Emir's Arena]] is built in the northern part of the [[Kharidian Empire]].{{CiteNPC|npc=Mubariz|quote=The original building was excavated by the Varrock Museum a while ago. It dated back to the Second Age!}}
*War breaks out between Kharidian and Zaros' expanding empire in the north,{{CiteNPC|npc=Mehhar|quote=It started during the rule of my grandmother. An ever-expanding empire to the north set their sights on our lands. War soon broke out.}} later known as the [[Kharidian–Zarosian War]].
**Icthlarin and Amascut lead the [[Mahjarrat]]{{CiteNPC|npc=Sphinx|quote=You clearly know little of Icthlarin and his past. Are you aware of the Mahjarrat? They once served Icthlarin, before they left him for Zamorak.||notes=They leave for Zaros, but Zaros is betrayed by Zamorak and some Mahjarrat.}} from their home plane [[Freneskae]]{{CiteNPC|npc=Mehhar|quote=They found them far from here, in a place beyond this world. A powerful race of faceless ones. They became Icthlarin's Stern Judges.|notes='They' refers to Icthlarin and Amascut.}} and shifted the war in the [[Menaphites]]' favour.{{CiteNPC|npc=Mehhar|quote=The armies of the Ruinous Powers were far stronger than our own. That was until Icthlarin's Stern Judges joined the fray. Thanks to them, the war was seemingly won.}}
**Amascut is warped into the being she is known as today,{{CiteNPC|npc=Mehhar|quote=Upon her return, Amascut vanished. She played no further part in the war. Only when the fighting was over did she reappear, but it wasn't really her at all.|loc=|notes=|name=}} The Devourer. This is believed to be caused by being exposed to the violence and rituals of the Mahjarrat both on Freneskae and back home.{{CiteNPC|npc=Mehhar|quote=It seems highly likely|notes=This is his anwser to the question: So you think it had something to do with the Stern Judges?}}
**The Mahjarrat betray Icthlarin and pledge their allegiance to [[Zaros]],{{CiteNPC|npc=Mehhar|loc=Beneath Cursed Sands|quote=Among the Stern Judges, there was a serpent. After my father [Osmumten] became Pharaoh, this serpent convinced the others to abandon us.}} continuing his war against the Menaphites.{{CiteNPC|npc=Mehhar|loc=Beneath Cursed Sands|quote=We were powerless against a force of that might. Nothing could stop their advance.}}
**Tumeken sacrifices himself to protect the Menaphite people, ending the war and obliterating most of the Mahjarrat, a loss the race never recovered from.{{CiteNPC|npc=Mehhar|loc=Beneath Cursed Sands|quote=[So how did the war end?] It was Tumeken himself. He sacrificed himself to annihilate the enemy. The cost was great, but the war was won.}}
*After the war, the [[Zarosian Empire]] reaches its peak, and [[Senntisten]] becomes the largest, most prosperous city in Gielinor, rivalling the elven city of [[Prifddinas]].
*[[Bandos]] arrives on Gielinor to wage war. He brings with him [[goblin (race)|goblins]], [[hobgoblin]]s, [[ogre]]s, [[ourg]]s, and various similar creatures to fight for him.
*The [[Saradomin]]ist kingdom, [[Hallowvale]], is founded in what is now eastern [[Morytania]].
*The [[Staff of Armadyl]] is recovered after having been lost for years.{{CiteNPC|npc=Valdez|quote=...but inside I located a great treasure... It was the godstaff of Armadyl. >> I chose that day to take it so that my Lord Saradomin's power...|loc=Curse of the Empty Lord}} It eventually ends up in the hands of [[Zamorak]].{{CiteNPC|npc=Rennard|quote=So I coshed this fella round the back of his head with me bag of jewels, picked up his package and was on me merry way afore he comes to.|loc=Curse of the Empty Lord|notes=Rennard robs Valdez of the staff, without knowing what it is.}}{{CiteNPC|npc=Kharrim|quote=Well anyway, when given the task of selling a weapon forged by the very gods themselves, I naturally thought of Zamorak as a potential buyer.|loc=Curse of the Empty Lord|note=Rennard tries to find a buyer for the to him generic weapon}}{{CiteNPC|npc=Viggora|quote=Myself and the rest of Zamoraks honour guard were formulating stratagems in our battle-tent, when that sneaky messenger Kharrim came in offering to sell us the god-staff of Armadyl!|loc=Curse of the Empty Lord}}
*Zamorak, a Mahjarrat general for Zaros at the time, organises his master's downfall.{{CiteNPC|npc=Viggora|quote=So anyway, Lord Zamorak and his most trusted compatriots, namely myself, Hazeel, Drakan, Thammaron and Zemouregal made plans to overthrow our lord using the god-weapon, and by pledging allegiance to Zamorak as our master, were each to be given a large piece of land as our own in return.|loc=Curse of the Empty Lord|notes=|name=}}
*Zamorak ascends to [[god]]hood after Zaros' defeat.{{CiteNPC|npc=Viggora|quote=Zamorak stood over the Empty Lord who was slowly... fading from existence... And as he faded, it seemed as though... It almost seemed as though Zamorak became more real|loc=Curse of the Empty Lord|notes=The decisive moment was when the Staff of Armadyl pierced both Zamorak and Zaros.}}

