{{Infobox Organisation
|name = Sect of Uhld
|image = [[File:Uhld emblem.png|250px]]
|release = [[4 January]] [[2018]]
|update = Dragon Slayer II
|founded = [[Fifth Age]]
|founder = [[Uhld]]
|leader = [[Alec Kincade]]
|headquarters = [[Myths' Guild]]
|location = [[Feldip Hills]]
}}
[[File:Myths' Guild.png|thumb|left|300px|The Myths' Guild, founded by the Sect of Uhld.]]
The '''Sect of Uhld''' are the founders of the [[Myths' Guild]].{{CiteNPC|npc=Erdan|quote=The Sect of Uhld, the founders of this here guild.}} [[Erdan]], a member of the guild, is a descendant of Uhld, the Sect's leader.{{CiteNPC|npc=Erdan|quote=I am Erdan, a descendant of Uhld.}}

Formerly a group of nomads residing somewhere in the southern coast of [[Feldip Hills]],{{CiteNPC|npc=Erdan|quote=...a nearby nomadic group called the Sect of Uhld were not pleased with the brutality they witnessed.}} they founded the guild sometime during the [[Runecrafting Crusades]] in the [[Fifth Age]] upon witnessing the destruction of the entrance to the [[Wrath Altar]], which had been rediscovered as a result of the wrath that the Fremennik crusaders, the Gunnites, had wrought upon the runic temples of the world.{{CiteNPC|npc=Erdan|quote=The story my father told me was of a war on magic, god fearing men who believed nothing good would come of wielding a power that was never meant for them. And so the rune temples that man had created were under threat, all were destroyed and thus forgotten, but the wrath that these Gunnites embraced rippled through the pocket dimensions and a new altar of power was discovered.}} Upon studying the rediscovered [[runic altar]], they were able to create [[surge spells]] and destroyed the Gunnites of the southern crusade.{{CiteNPC|npc=Erdan|quote=...the Sect of Uhld had used the information gained from the wrath altar, and with a spell of their own making, they destroyed the southern runecrafting crusade with much ease.}}

The Sect's primary goal in founding the Myths' Guild was information preservation,{{CiteNPC|npc=Erdan|quote=Quickly they [the Sect] established this guild with information preservation as their core goal, for men are recorders of history and magic is key for this to last.}} as well as distinguishing fact and myths throughout history, all of which are archived in the guild's Library of Knowledge.{{CiteNPC|npc=Alec Kincade|quote=As time passes, that which was once fact, becomes myth. Some tales are just that, tales. However, some tales are something more. Here at the Myths' Guild, we live to tell the difference between the two. If you wish to join us, you must do the same.}}

