|id = 6448
}}
The '''secure chest''' is a chest that is opened with a [[lockpick]] during [[Desert Treasure I]]. Opening this chest requires 53 [[Thieving]], successfully opening it gives 150 [[Thieving]] experience and yields the [[Gilded cross]].

The chest has 3 locks, all of which must be unlocked in a row to open the chest. Failing to open one of the locks causes all the locks to reset, breaks the lockpick and deals 2-3 one-time damage to the player. It may also apply up to 6 points of recurrent poison damage on the player. After successfully unlocking this chest, it remains unlocked and can be opened without a lockpick.

The nearby [[Bandit (Bandit Camp)|Bandits]] may be pickpocketed for lockpicks and [[antipoison(1)]] potions.

==Success chance==
The chance of successfully opening the secure chest is 52/256 at level 1, and 128/256 at level 99, interpolating linearly in between.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1149240089316380672|date=11 July 2019|archiveurl=https://archive.vn/U1BO4|archivedate=2 February 2021|quote=[The chance of success at the secure chest] is 20.4% at level 1 (if that were allowed), 50.2% at level 99, interpolating linearly between.|notes=|name=|group=}}

