{{External|rs=Seers' ring}} {{Infobox Item |name = Seers ring |image = [[File:Seers ring.png]] |release = [[7 November]] [[2005]] |update = Waterbirth Island - deeper, darker, deadlier! |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Wear, Drop |examine = A mysterious ring that can fill the wearer with magical power... |value = 10000 |weight = 0.004 |exchange = Yes |id = 6731 |leagueRegion = Fremennik }} [[File:Seers ring detail.png|left|155px]] The '''Seers ring''' is one of the four [[Fremennik rings]], and is dropped by the [[Dagannoth Prime]] in the [[Waterbirth Island Dungeon]].
It can be [[Seers ring (i)|imbued]] using 650,000 [[Nightmare Zone]] reward points or 325,000 with the [[Combat_Achievements/Hard|hard tier]] of [[Combat Achievements]], 260 [[Soul Wars]] [[Zeal Tokens]], or a [[Scroll of imbuing|Scroll of Imbuing]], purchased for 200 [[Emir's Arena]] reward points, which doubles the magic attack and defence bonuses, and increases the magic damage bonus from 0.2% to 0.5%.
Players can use a [[chisel]] on the seers ring to create a [[seers icon]] after completing [[Desert Treasure II]]. This process requires 80 [[Crafting]] (boostable), and is part of the process for creating the [[magus ring]].
