{{External|rs}} {{Infobox NPC |version1 = Female |version2 = Male (unused/removed) |name = Servant |image1 = [[File:Servant (ScapeRune, female).png|120px]] |image2 = [[File:Servant (ScapeRune, male).png|120px]] |release = [[9 August]] [[2005]] |update = Tai Bwo Wannai Clean-Up |removal1 = No |removal2 = October [[2006]] |members = No |race = [[Human]] |location = [[ScapeRune]] |gender1 = Female |gender2 = Male |options = Talk-to |examine = Servant of Evil Bob. |map1 = {{Map|x=2527|y=4777|plane=0|r=4|mapID=-1|mtype=square}} |map2 = No |id1 = 393 |id2 = hist392 |leagueRegion1 = General |leagueRegion2 = No }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Servant (ScapeRune, female) chathead.png|left]] |version2 = [[File:Servant (ScapeRune, male) chathead.png|left]] }} The '''Servant''' is a human [[Non-player character|NPC]] that appears only on [[ScapeRune|Evil Bob's Island]] in the [[ScapeRune]] dimension. The Servant helps the players to escape the island, by showing them where to fish for the [[fish-like thing]] that is required to put [[Evil Bob]] to sleep.
Having given Evil Bob the fish and seen him fall asleep, the player can urge the servant to come with them back to [[Gielinor]].
When refused, female players to the servant would say, "Oh, alright then", but male players to the servant had the option to admit their love for the servant saying "But I love you!", however she would still remain reluctant to leave saying "Our love cannot be". After an [[Diversity & Inclusion updates|update aimed at diversity and inclusion]], players of any gender are now able to confess their love to the servant.
==Dialogue== {{Hastranscript|npc}}
==Trivia== *A male servant could also be seen on the island when the event was first released. He was removed for unknown reasons in late 2006, and has therefore never been present in ''Old School RuneScape''; he remained in the game files until the [[2024 Pride event]], where he was removed.
