{{Infobox NPC |name = Servius, Teokan of Ralos |image = [[File:Servius, Teokan of Ralos.png|120px]] |release = [[10 January]] [[2024]] |update = Children of the Sun |members = Yes |race = [[Human]] |quest = [[Children of the Sun]], [[Twilight's Promise]], [[The Heart of Darkness]] |location = Crypt underneath Fortis temple, [[The Teomat]], [[Sunrise Palace]] |gender = Male |options = Talk-to |examine = Leader of the Church of Ralos. |map = No |id = 12652,12899,12900,12901,13694,14307,14374,14377 |leagueRegion = Varlamore }} [[File:Servius, Teokan of Ralos chathead.png|left]] '''Servius''' is the [[Teokan]], or high priest, of the Church of [[Ralos]] and the father of [[Prince Itzla Arkan]].
==History== ===Early History=== Servius is the current Teokan of the Church of Ralos. As the Teokan, an old Varlamorian tradition states that the current ruler of Varlamore should unite with a Teokan of Ralos, as they would need the guidance of Ralos' light the most. [[Queen Zyanyi Arkan]] was willing to revive this tradition, which Servius accepted, and the two had a son named Itzla.{{CiteNPC|npc=Servius, Teokan of Ralos|quote=We are incredibly close, for we are united in Ralos' light, and in the love we share for Itzla. However, it would be fair to say that our relationship is not a conventional one, especially to an outsider. [Player: So how did it come about?] In times of old, the ruler of Varlamore would often unite with a Teokan of Ralos. His light guides us in all things, and a King or Queen will need that guidance more than most. Before she took the throne, the Queen made the decision to revive that old tradition. I was more than happy to accept.|loc=The Final Dawn}} Itzla describes his familial relations to them as being "a convoluted mess".{{CiteNPC|npc=Prince Itzla Arkan|quote=I don't believe you've properly met my father. This is Servius, the Teokan of Ralos and the man whose life you saved. [Player: Your father? I didn't realise you were related.] Yes, very fun stuff. All a bit of a convoluted mess as well!|loc=Twilight's Promise}}
When Varlamore decided to open to the rest of Gielinor, Servius was sent to meet with [[King Roald]] of [[Varrock]]. A passing adventurer caught wind of a plot by several bandits who were hired to assassinate him, foiling the attempt. The meeting went on without any issues and the Varlamore delegation returned to their lands.
===Inside Troubles=== Wondering who was behind the plot against his father, Itzla asked the adventurer to help him find the true culprit. Servius met with the adventurer for the first time, thanking them for saving his life from the would-be assassins. Itzla believed that the Tullus twins, [[Ennius Tullus|Ennius]] and [[Furia Tullus|Furia]], were worth investigating. Since the orders came from someone in the delegation, the adventurer was tasked with finding the suspect, while Servius decided to return to the Teomat, despite Itzla's concerns that it was not as safe as the palace. At the Teomat, Servius spoke with [[Metzli]], after which several [[Cultist]]s of the [[Twilight Emissaries]] attacked. In the ensuing chaos, Servius was stabbed in the chest, likely by Metzli. Servius was quickly taken into intensive care following the incident.
With the Twilight Emissaries becoming a larger threat, Itzla and the adventurer infiltrated the cult in order to discern its workings, and were led to the [[Old Ones]] fortress of the [[Ruins of Tapoyauik]], learning from the [[Frost Nagua]] [[Amoxliatl]] that the cult sought the Mokhaiotl, the Tlati archive. Having trailed the two, the Emissaries forcibly teleported Itzla away and left the adventurer behind to face Amoxliatl's wrath. The adventurer defeated the nagua and was subsequently banished by her, returning to Fortis to inform the authorities. There, they found Servius had made a full recovery and told him of Itzla's kidnapping by the cult.
Upon learning the treachery of Metzli and the Tullus twins, Servius declared that they would burn in the light of Ralos for their actions. He also learned that they sought [[Mokhaiotl]], causing him to consider them as lost fools and told them to not trust a nagua's words. With these developments, he would seek Ralos' guidance and would inform Queen Zyanyi of the news, promising to call for their aid when the time came.
