{{Infobox Organisation
|name = Seven Priestly Warriors
|image = [[File:Priest in Peril.png]]
|release = [[29 June]] [[2004]]
|update = Priest In Peril Quest
|founded = ~1200 [[Fourth Age]]
|location = [[Misthalin]]
}}
'''The Seven Priestly Warriors''' is a term widely applied to [[Ivandis Seergaze]], [[Iriandul Caistlyn]], [[Sarl Dunegun]], [[Derygull Templeton]], [[Erysail the Pious]], [[Friar Twiblick]], and [[Essiandar Gar]], [[Temple Knights]] that defended [[Misthalin]] and [[Asgarnia]] from invading [[Morytania]]n forces during the [[Misthalin - Morytania War]], in roughly 1200 of the [[Fourth Age]].{{CiteText|text=Varrock Museum#1st_floor2nd_floor_Display_cases{{!}}Varrock Museum Timeline exhibit, display number 23|quote=4th Age - yr 1100-1200. A tide of evil creatures from the east threatened Avarrocka (…). Seven priestly warriors - Iriandul Caistlyn, Sarl Dunegun, Friar Twiblick, Derygull, Ivandis Seergaze, Erysail the Pious and Essiandar Gar - attempted to drive the evil creatures back into what we now know as Morytania.}} They fought at [[Silvarea]], upon which the [[Paterdomus]] was constructed after their death in battle.{{CiteNPC|npc=Drezel|loc=Priest in Peril|quote=The temple here was built soon after. It guards the source of the River Salve, and acts as the only passage between Misthalin and Morytania.}} Of them, only Ivandis Seergaze of [[Lumbridge]] survived the direct conflict with [[Lord Drakan]]'s forces, although he himself died during a later venture into the region.{{CiteNPC|npc=Veliaf Hurtz|loc=In Aid of the Myreque|quote=He supposedly led countless charges into Morytania and ultimately perished somewhere within these lands.}}

The warriors also blessed the [[River Salve]] during the final battle of the Misthalin - Morytania War, creating a barrier to prevent Morytanian invasion in the future.{{CiteText|text=The Sleeping Seven|quote=As the priestly brothers and sisters fought on, some of them cast blessings into the Salve and sealed in it the vengeful power of Saradomin who would act as Misthalin's guardian against 'his-dark- self'.|page=14}} This blessing has held, although there have been several instances of crossing through various methods. The warriors remain some of [[human]]ity's most universally celebrated historical figures, although they are most frequently referenced in [[Misthalin|Misthalinian]] lore and history.

