{{Infobox Item |name = Shadow blocker |image = [[File:Shadow blocker.png]] |release = [[26 July]] [[2023]] |update = Desert Treasure II - The Fallen Empire |members = Yes |quest = [[Desert Treasure II - The Fallen Empire]] |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Place, Destroy |destroy = You might be able to get another from Ketla's workbench in the Lassar Undercity. |examine = Keeps the shadows at bay. |value = 30 |alchable = No |weight = 3.000 |id = 28367 }} [[File:Shadow blocker detail.png|left|100px]] The '''shadow blocker''' is an item used during [[Desert Treasure II - The Fallen Empire]], where it is obtained by searching [[Ketla]]'s workbench in her house in the [[Lassar Undercity]]'s Residential District after giving her the [[shadow blocker schematic]].
When placed in the Undercity, being next to it will protect the player's [[sanity]] when they enter the [[Shadow Realm]]. When players exit the Shadow Realm, the [[blackstone fragment]] can recall it back to the player's inventory from wherever they were placed.
{{Desert Treasure II - The Fallen Empire}}

{{Infobox Combat Achievement |name = Shadow dancer |image = [[File:Yama.png|200px]] |release = [[29 May]] [[2025]] |update = Yama CAs & More! |members = Yes |description = Defeat Yama without getting hit by shadows and without being more than one tile away from the center<!--sic--> of his shadow crash attack. |tier = Master |monster = Yama |type = Mechanical |id = 605 |leagueRegion = Kourend }} '''Shadow dancer''' is a [[Combat Achievements/Master|master combat achievement]] which requires the player to defeat [[Yama]] without getting hit by shadows and without being more than one tile away from the centre of his shadow crash attack.
{{Bug|Although reportedly claimed to be fixed, it is still possible to get hit by the Shadow Waves while in the phase transition teleport animation, failing the CA.}}
==Strategy== The achievement requires that the player avoid the following: * Taking damage from ranged attacks off-prayer * Taking damage from shadow-based special attacks in phases 1 and 2 * Taking damage from Shadow Waves * Taking damage from Shadow Crash * Being more than one tile away from the centre fireball during the Shadow Crash attack
In a duo fight, a player failing this achievement will not cause their partner to fail.
<gallery mode="packed" heights="200" style="text-align:left"> Yama - dodging shadow flame wall.mp4|A pair of players skip over the shadow waves. Yama - phase 3 dodging.mp4|Players avoid both the shadow crash and shadow wave during the final phase of the fight. </gallery>
