{{External|rs|dw=Shadow Sword}} {{Infobox Item |name = Shadow sword |image = [[File:Shadow sword.png]] |release = [[12 February]] [[2007]] |update = A sq'irk a day... |members = Yes |quest = [[The General's Shadow]] |tradeable = No |equipable = Yes |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Wield, Destroy |destroy = You can get another one by visiting the cave near the Fishing guild. A friendly ghost will replace it for you. |examine = A shadow sword. |value = 0 |weight = 3.628 |id = 10858 }}
[[File:Shadow sword detail.png|left|100px]] The '''shadow sword''' is a two-handed sword obtained as a reward from [[The General's Shadow]] mini-quest. The sword matches the [[ghostly robes]] set, though it cannot be stored alongside the robes in the [[costume room]] of a [[player-owned house]].
The shadow sword has the same stats as a [[black 2h sword]], with additional [[Magic]] attack and defence bonuses.
If lost, the sword can be reclaimed by speaking to the [[Ghost (The General's Shadow)|ghost]] in the room where you fought [[Bouncer (ghost)|Bouncer's ghost]] (accessible through a crack on the south wall of the north-eastern room in the [[Goblin Cave|Goblin Cave]], just east of the [[Fishing Guild|Fishing Guild]] entrance). A [[ghostspeak amulet]] (or [[Morytania legs 2]] or better) must be worn in order to talk to the ghost.
The ghost will not give you a second copy if you already have one in your inventory or bank. The only way to obtain multiple copies at the same time is to first deposit one in the master [[STASH|STASH unit]] in the south-east corner of [[Zamorak's Fortress]].
Note: Despite being untradeable, the shadow sword will '''always''' be lost on death, unless it's one of the three (or four with [[Protect Item]]) items protected on death. It will also not appear on the ground, meaning you will have to reclaim it.
