{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Shaikahan bones |image = [[File:Shaikahan bones.png]] |release = [[14 September]] [[2004]] |update = Tai Bwo Wannai Trio |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |options = Bury, Drop |examine = Large glistening bones which glow with a pale yellow aura. |value = 1 |weight = 1.500 |exchange = Yes |id = 3123 }} [[File:Shaikahan bones detail.png|left|150px]] '''Shaikahan bones''' are dropped by [[The Shaikahan]] when it is killed, which requires a [[Karambwan paste]]-poisoned [[spear]] or [[hasta]]. Note that any kills prior to [[Tai Bwo Wannai Trio]] will not yield any bones. Despite the examine text stating it glows with a yellow aura, its appearance remains akin to that of dragon bones.
Shaikahan bones give 25 [[Prayer]] experience when buried. This can be increased by offering the bones in different ways: * 75 XP when casting [[Sinister Offering]]. * 75 XP when offered at the [[Sacred Bone Burner]] after the appropriate faith level has been achieved. * 87.5 XP when offered at a [[gilded altar]] with two burners lit or at the [[Chaos Temple (hut)|Chaos Temple]]. * 100 XP when offered at the [[Ectofuntus]] in the form of [[Shaikahan bonemeal]].
