{{Gone|update=Children of the Sun}} [[File:Shayzien supply set (1) detail.png|left|130x200px]] '''Shayzien supply armour''' was the non-equipable version of [[Shayzien armour]]. Unlike Shayzien armour, Shayzien supply armour could be smithed, but was not useable/equipable by players.
The [[Shayzien supply crate|crate]] for the armour had to be collected by searching the drawers in any of the armourer's buildings, and was found in noted form. Players would need to exchange this banknote for a crate, then 'pack' the crate in order to hand in armour sets in bulk for experience and/or Lovakengj favour.
Shayzien supply armour was made from [[lovakite bar]]s, which '''must''' be smelted in the [[lovakite furnace]] from 2 [[coal]] and 1 [[lovakite ore]], or using [[Superheat Item]]. One full set of armour took 11 bars to smith. Players could create and deliver Shayzien supply armour and Shayzien supply sets to [[armourer]]s in exchange for [[Mining]] and [[Smithing]] [[experience]], as well as [[Lovakengj favour]]. Each tier of filled crate gave the same amount of Mining experience, but higher tiers did grant additional Smithing experience and [[favour]]. Handing in a set rewarded 36.5% more favour and experience for Mining and Smithing than handing in all 5 pieces of the same tier not packed into a set.
According to the [[armourer]]s who coordinated the manufacturing process of the armours, they supply the armours to the [[Shayzien Army]] in exchange for protection due to the lack of combat prowess possessed by the Lovakengj [[dwarves]].
Following the removal of the favour system, smithing Shayzien supply armour was replaced with smithing equipable Shayzien armour. {| class="wikitable" |+ ! colspan="7" |30% Favour to 75% - 100% Favour |- !Smithing Level !Tier 1 Sets !Tier 2 Sets !Tier 3 Sets !Tier 4 Sets !75% Bars Required !100% Bars Required |- |53+ |30 sets | | | |330 |517 (+17 sets) |- |63+ |7 sets |12 sets | | |209 |297 (+8 sets) |- |'''73+''' |'''7 sets''' |'''4 sets''' |'''5 sets''' | |'''176''' |'''242 (+6 sets)''' |- |83+ |7 sets |4 sets |2 sets |3 sets |176 |220 (+4 sets) |- |93+ |7 sets |4 sets |2 sets |3 sets |176 |209 (+3 Tier 5 sets) |} ''*Recommended to stop at Tier 3 armour sets for 75% favour. When going for 100% favour the additional effort of turning in the previous sets might not be worth the small time savings of smelting 22-33 additional ores.''
''*small difference in number of ores needed at higher tiers when factoring in turning in individual pieces. only notable mention is for 83+ where you only need 2 tier 4 sets and a tier 4 platebody for 75% favour.''
{| class="wikitable" |- !!!Mining experience!!Smithing experience !Smithing Level!!Favour gained |- |Tier 1 Armour||45 per bar used||80 per bar used |45 through 53||0.1% per bar used |- |Tier 1 Set||675||1,200 |53||1.5% |- |Tier 2 Armour||45 per bar used||100 per bar used |55 through 63||0.2% per bar used |- |Tier 2 Set||675||1,500 |63||3% |- |Tier 3 Armour||45 per bar used||120 per bar used |65 through 73||0.3% per bar used |- |Tier 3 Set||675||1,800 |73||4.5% |- |Tier 4 Armour||45 per bar used||140 per bar used |75 through 83||0.4% per bar used |- |Tier 4 Set||675||2,100 |83||6% |- |Tier 5 Armour||45 per bar used||160 per bar used |85 through 93||0.5% per bar used |- |Tier 5 Set||675||2,400 |93||7.5% |}
