{{External|rs}} {{Infobox Item |name = Shield fragment |image = [[File:Shield fragment.png]] |release = [[24 April]] [[2007]] |update = Another Slice of H.A.M. |members = Yes |quest = [[Another Slice of H.A.M.]] |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options = Drop |destroy = ''You drop the artefact and it rolls back to its original place in the ground.'' |examine = A piece of an ancient goblin shield. |value = 1 |alchable = No |weight = 0.001 |id = 11054 }} [[File:Shield fragment detail.png|left|150px]] The '''shield fragment''' is a [[quest item]] in the [[Another Slice of H.A.M.]] [[quest]]. It is one of the six [[artefact]]s obtained during the first stage of the quest by digging with a [[trowel]] in the unfinished train tunnel in [[Dorgesh-Kaan]].
When the artefacts are cleaned using a [[specimen brush]], one turns into the shield fragment, which must be given to [[Tegdak]], the cave goblin, along with the other cleaned artefacts: a [[helmet fragment]], an [[armour shard]], a [[sword fragment]], and an [[ancient mace]].
[[Alchemy]] spells cannot be cast on them, attempting to do so results in the chatbox saying: ''"This ancient artefact resists your magic."''
