{{External|rs|rsc=Shrimp}} {{Otheruses|cooked shrimps|the raw version|raw shrimps}} {{Infobox Item |name = Shrimps |image = [[File:Shrimps.png]] |release = [[11 June]] [[2001]] |update = New fishing skill and more cooking |members = No |quest = No |tradeable = Yes |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = Yes |edible = Yes |options = Eat, Drop |examine = Some nicely cooked shrimp. |value = 5 |weight = 0.100 |exchange = Yes |id = 315 }} [[File:Shrimps detail.png|left|100px]] '''Shrimp''' is a type of fish that restores 3 [[Hitpoints]] when eaten. It can be obtained by cooking [[raw shrimp]] on a [[fire]] or [[cooking range]], granting 30 [[experience]] when successful. When cooking there is a chance to fail, resulting in [[burnt shrimp]]. The [[burn rate]] decreases as the player's [[Cooking]] level increases. Shrimp is one of a number of foods with a reduced burn rate while using the [[Cooking range (Lumbridge Castle)|Lumbridge Castle range]] with [[Cook's Assistant]] completed. It will stop burning entirely at Cooking level 34, or 31 when using the Lumbridge range.
Shrimp are one of the fish required by [[Caleb]] in the quest [[Family Crest]].
[[Rick]] can make shrimps for the player in a [[player-owned house]].
