{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of eternal belief |image1 = [[File:Sigil of eternal belief.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of eternal belief (attuned).png]] |release = [[21 January]] [[2026]] |update = Holy Moleys and the Hooded Slayer Helm are Here! |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |bankable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Unlock, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = |examine1 = Prayer does not drain naturally, but your prayer can still be affected by prayer drain effects like smite. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |alchable = No |weight = 0.100 |id1 = 33060 |id2 = 33059 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of eternal belief detail.png|130px|left]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of eternal belief (attuned) detail.png|130px|left]] }} The '''Sigil of Eternal Belief''' is a utility sigil in [[Deadman: Annihilation]]. It is a permanent unlock that makes it so [[Prayer points]] do not drain naturally. However, Prayer can still be drained by prayer-draining effects like [[Smite]], [[shadow spider]]s, [[Barrows]], or attempting to steal [[Wine of Zamorak|wines of Zamorak]] from the Chaos Temple in Asgarnia or the Wilderness. This can be useful for players looking to complete certain diary tasks which require the player to restore prayer points.
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], it can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune'' and is a permanent unlock. There is no limit on how many permanent sigils can be active at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using it on the [[deadman's skull]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |[[Prayer points|Prayer]] does not drain naturally, but your prayer can still be affected by prayer drain effects like [[smite]]. |}
{{Deadman: Annihilation}}

{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of faith |image1 = [[File:Sigil of faith.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of faith (attuned).png]] |release = [[23 August]] [[2023]] |update = Deadman: Apocalypse - Friday 25th August |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Unlock, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = You always gain twice the number of Prayer Points when consuming Prayer-restoring potions. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |alchable = No |weight = 0.400 |id1 = 28520 |id2 = 28519 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of faith detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of faith (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of Faith''' is a tier 2 utility [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. It is a permanent unlock that yields twice the number of [[Prayer points]] when drinking [[Prayer#Consumables|Prayer-restoring potions]].
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], it can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune'' and is a permanent unlock. There is no limit on how many permanent sigils can be active at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using it on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |You always gain twice the number of [[Prayer points]] when consuming [[Prayer#Consumables|Prayer-restoring potions]]. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |You have a 40% chance to gain twice the number of Prayer points when consuming Prayer-restoring potions. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |You have a 20% chance to gain twice the number of Prayer points when consuming Prayer-restoring potions. |}
