{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of the alchemaniac |image1 = [[File:Sigil of the alchemaniac.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of the alchemaniac (attuned).png]] |release = [[23 August]] [[2023]] |update = Deadman: Apocalypse - Friday 25th August |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Unlock, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = When casting high or low alchemy on a stack of items, the spell will automatically recast over time, until the stack is depleted or moved. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |alchable = No |weight = 0.400 |id1 = 28484 |id2 = 28483 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of the alchemaniac detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of the alchemaniac (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of the Alchemaniac''' is a tier 1 utility [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. It is a permanent unlock that automatically recasts [[High Level Alchemy|high]] or [[Low Level Alchemy|low alchemy]] on a stack of items. It does ''not'' remove the [[Magic]] level requirement for the spells or the [[rune]]s required to cast the spells.
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], it can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune'' and is a permanent unlock. There is no limit on how many permanent sigils can be active at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using it on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |When casting [[High Level Alchemy|high]] or [[Low Level Alchemy|low alchemy]] on a stack of items, the spell will automatically recast over time, until the stack is depleted or moved. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |High Level Alchemy will provide 30% extra coins. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |High Level Alchemy will provide 30% extra coins. |- |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |When casting high or low alchemy on a stack of items, the spell will automatically recast over time, until the stack is depleted or moved. |}
{{Deadman: Annihilation}} {{Deadman: Armageddon}} {{Deadman: Apocalypse}}

