{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of the gunslinger |image1 = [[File:Sigil of gunslinger.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of gunslinger (attuned).png]] |release = [[17 July]] [[2024]] |update = Deadman: Armageddon & While Guthix Sleeps Updates |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable1 = No |tradeable2 = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Attune, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Inspect, Unattune, Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = All ranged weapons with a base attack speed above 4 will have it reduced by 1. Cannot be used in conjunction with the Sigil of the Swashbuckler or the Sigil of Arcane Swiftness. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |weight = 0.100 |id1 = 29676 |id2 = 29675 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of gunslinger detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of gunslinger (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of the Gunslinger''' is a tier 2 [[Deadman Mode]] combat sigil. It is an attunable sigil that reduces the [[attack speed]] of 4-tick on rapid (5-tick on accurate/longrange) or slower [[Ranged]] weapons by 1. It cannot be used with the [[Sigil of the Swashbuckler]] or the [[Sigil of Arcane Swiftness]]. Additionally, the [[crystal bow]], [[Bow of Faerdhinen]], and [[Morrigan's thrownaxe]] '''do not''' benefit from the sigil.
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], the un-attuned version can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune''. Up to three attunable sigils can be attuned at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using them on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |All ranged weapons with a base attack speed above 4 will have it reduced by 1. Cannot be used in conjunction with the [[Sigil of the Swashbuckler]] or the [[Sigil of Arcane Swiftness]]. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |All ranged weapons with a base attack speed above 4 will have it reduced by 1. |}
==Changes== {{Subject changes header}} {{Subject changes |date = 21 January 2026 |update = Holy Moleys and the Hooded Slayer Helm are Here! |change = The item was renamed from Sigil of gunslinger to Sigil of the gunslinger. }} {{Subject changes footer}}
[[File:Sigil of the gunslinger icon.png|left|thumb|The icon for the sigil of gunslinger.]]
{{Deadman: Annihilation}} {{Deadman: Armageddon}}

{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of the hunter |image1 = [[File:Sigil of the hunter.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of the hunter (attuned).png]] |release = [[23 August]] [[2023]] |update = Deadman: Apocalypse - Friday 25th August |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Attune, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = You gain three chinchompas per successful chinchompa capture. Box traps catch chinchompas faster. Hunter catching will rarely fail. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |alchable = No |weight = 0.400 |id1 = 28487 |id2 = 28486 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of the hunter detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of the hunter (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of the Hunter''' is a tier 2 skilling [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. It is a permanent unlock that gives additional [[Chinchompa (disambiguation)|chinchompas]] when using [[box trap]]s, as well as speeds up box traps and gives an increased catch rate for [[Hunter]] actions.
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], it can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune'' and is a permanent unlock. There is no limit on how many permanent sigils can be active at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using it on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |You gain three [[Chinchompa (disambiguation)|chinchompas]] per successful chinchompa capture. [[Box trap]]s catch chinchompas faster. Hunter catching will rarely fail. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |You gain three Chinchompas per successful Chinchompa capture. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |You gain three Chinchompas per successful Chinchompa capture. |}
{{Deadman: Annihilation}} {{Deadman: Armageddon}} {{Deadman: Apocalypse}}

{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of the infernal chef |image1 = [[File:Sigil of the infernal chef.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of the infernal chef (attuned).png]] |release = [[23 August]] [[2023]] |update = Deadman: Apocalypse - Friday 25th August |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Unlock, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = You have a 50% chance to instantly cook fish that are caught while Fishing, granting Cooking XP regardless of level requirements. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 10000 |alchable = No |weight = 0.400 |id1 = 28502 |id2 = 28501 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of the infernal chef detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of the infernal chef (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of the Infernal Chef''' is a tier 2 skilling [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. It is a permanent unlock that gives a 50% chance to instantly cook fish that are caught while Fishing. This grants Cooking experience regardless of whether or not the player has the Cooking level required to cook the fish normally.
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], it can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune'' and is a permanent unlock. There is no limit on how many permanent sigils can be active at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using it on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |You have a 50% chance to instantly cook fish that are caught while Fishing, granting Cooking XP regardless of level requirements. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |Provides a 20% chance to instantly cook fish that are caught while Fishing, granting Cooking experience regardless of level requirements. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |Instantly cook [[fish]] that are caught while [[Fishing]], granting [[Cooking]] experience regardless of level requirements. |}
{{Deadman: Annihilation}} {{Deadman: Armageddon}} {{Deadman: Apocalypse}}

{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of the infernal smith |image1 = [[File:Sigil of the infernal smith.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of the infernal smith (attuned).png]] |release = [[23 August]] [[2023]] |update = Deadman: Apocalypse - Friday 25th August |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Attune, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Inspect, Unattune, Destroy |destroy1 = An alternative is to sell it on the Grand Exchange. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = A power enhancing sigil not yet attuned to you. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |alchable = No |weight = 0.400 |exchange1 = dmm |exchange2 = No |id1 = 28505 |id2 = 28504 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of the infernal smith detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of the infernal smith (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of the infernal smith''' is a tier 2 skilling [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. Like all sigils, the un-attuned version is dropped by most monsters (via the [[Deadman:_Apocalypse/Global_loot_table|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and is tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune''.
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |You have a 20% chance to instantly forge bars from the ore you mine, granting Smithing experience regardless of level requirements. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |Instantly forge [[bars]] from the [[ore]] you mine, granting [[Smithing]] experience regardless of level requirements. |}
=== Examples ===
* Ores that require [[coal]] are forged into the appropriate bar (e.g. [[mithril ore]] will be forged into a [[mithril bar]] without any [[coal]])
* [[Iron ore]] will be forged into [[Steel bar|steel bars]] * [[Tin ore|Tin]] or [[copper ore]] will be forged into [[Bronze bar|bronze bars]] {{Deadman: Armageddon}} {{Deadman: Apocalypse}}

{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of the lightbearer |image1 = [[File:Sigil of the lightbearer.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of the lightbearer (attuned).png]] |release = [[23 August]] [[2023]] |update = Deadman: Apocalypse - Friday 25th August |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Attune, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Inspect, Unattune, Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = Special attack regeneration will become 15 seconds per 10%. If a lightbearer ring is also equipped, special attack regeneration will become 10 seconds per 10%. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |alchable = No |weight = 0.400 |id1 = 28508 |id2 = 28507 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of the lightbearer detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of the lightbearer (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of the Lightbearer''' is a tier 2 combat [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. It is an attunable sigil that increases [[special attack]] energy regeneration to 15 seconds per 10%. When combined with the [[Lightbearer]], the rate of regeneration becomes 10 seconds per 10%.
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], the un-attuned version can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune''. Up to three attunable sigils can be attuned at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using them on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |[[Special attack]] regeneration will become 15 seconds per 10%. If a [[Lightbearer|lightbearer ring]] is also equipped, special attack regeneration will become 10 seconds per 10%. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |Special attack regeneration will become 15 seconds per 10%. If a Lightbearer ring is also equipped, special attack regeneration will become 10 seconds per 10%. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |Special attack regeneration will become 15 seconds per 10%. If a Lightbearer ring is also equipped, special attack regeneration will become 10 seconds per 10%. |}
{{Deadman: Annihilation}} {{Deadman: Armageddon}} {{Deadman: Apocalypse}}

{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of the menacing mage |image1 = [[File:Sigil of the menacing mage.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of the menacing mage (attuned).png]] |release = [[25 August]] [[2021]] |update = Deadman: Reborn |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable1 = No |tradeable2 = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Attune, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Inspect, Unattune, Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = Upon dealing magic damage, you have a 15% chance to curse the target. The curse deals 18 damage (33% less damage in 3-60 worlds) over the next 6 seconds and also heals you for the same amount. A target can only be under the effect of one curse at a time. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |weight = 0.100 |id1 = 26078 |id2 = 26077 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of the menacing mage detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of the menacing mage (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of the Menacing Mage''' is a tier 2 combat [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. It is the basic [[Magic]] sigil and can be chosen for free as a starting sigil in [[Deadman: Annihilation]] or purchased for [[Deadman: Annihilation/Points|points]] thereafter. It gives a chance to curse a target when dealing magic damage, dealing damage over time that also heals the caster. The damage over time is reduced in the lowest combat bracket worlds. It is an attunable sigil.
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], the un-attuned version can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune''. Up to three attunable sigils can be attuned at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using them on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |Upon dealing magic damage, you have a 15% chance to curse the target. The curse deals 18 damage (33% less damage in 3-60 worlds) over the next 6 seconds and also heals you for the same amount. A target can only be under the effect of one curse at a time. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |Upon dealing Magic damage, you have a 10% chance to curse the target. The curse deals 18 damage, 33% less damage in the 3 to 50 bracket, over the next 6 seconds and heals you for the same amount. A target can only be under the effect of one curse at a time. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |Upon dealing Magic damage, you have a 20% chance to curse the target. The curse deals 12 damage over the next 6 seconds and heals you for the same amount. A target can only be under the effect of one curse at a time. |- |[[Deadman: Reborn]] |Upon dealing Magic damage, you have a 20% chance to curse the target. The curse deals 12 damage over the next 6 seconds and heals you for the same amount. A target can only be under the effect of one curse at a time. You also gain an additional 50% XP in the Magic skill. |}
