{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of the treasure hunter |image1 = [[File:Sigil of the treasure hunter.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of the treasure hunter (attuned).png]] |release = [[25 August]] [[2021]] |update = Deadman: Reborn |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable1 = No |tradeable2 = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Unlock, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = Clue scrolls drop 3x more often. You have a 75% chance for a clue scroll to return the reward casket after you complete a clue step for any tier. You can hold an unlimited amount of Scroll boxes. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |weight = 0.100 |id1 = 26051 |id2 = 26050 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of the treasure hunter detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of the treasure hunter (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of the Treasure Hunter''' is a tier 1 utility [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. It is a permanent unlock that increases the rate of [[clue scroll]] drops, as well as offers a chance for every clue step to return the [[reward casket]]. It also allows holding an unlimited number of [[scroll box]]es.
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], it can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune'' and is a permanent unlock. There is no limit on how many permanent sigils can be active at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using it on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
This sigil only affects [[clue scroll]]s dropped by NPCs, not those obtained through [[Thieving|pickpocketing]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |[[Clue scroll]]s drop 3x more often. You have a 75% chance for a clue scroll to return the reward casket after you complete a clue step for any tier. You can hold an unlimited amount of [[scroll box]]es. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |Clue Scrolls drop 3x more often. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |Clue Scrolls drop 2x more often. |- |[[Deadman: Reborn]] |Clue Scrolls drop 2x more often. |}
