{{Deadman seasonal}} {{Infobox Item |version1 = Un-attuned |version2 = Attuned |name = Sigil of woodcraft |image1 = [[File:Sigil of woodcraft.png]] |image2 = [[File:Sigil of woodcraft (attuned).png]] |release = [[23 August]] [[2023]] |update = Deadman: Apocalypse - Friday 25th August |members = Yes |quest = No |tradeable1 = No |tradeable2 = No |equipable = No |stackable = No |noteable = No |options1 = Unlock, Inspect, Destroy |options2 = Destroy |destroy1 = You can sell duplicate sigils by using them on Deadman's skull. |destroy2 = You must unattune the Sigil before you can destroy it. |examine1 = Instead of receiving logs when chopping specific trees, you will receive the appropriate planks. Requires 50 coins per regular plank, 125 coins per oak plank, 250 coins per teak plank, and 700 coins per mahogany plank. Does not work in guarded areas or with the infernal axe. |examine2 = A sigil attuned to you with great power. |value = 1 |alchable = No |weight = 0.400 |id1 = 28529 |id2 = 28528 }} {{Synced switch |version1 = [[File:Sigil of woodcraft detail.png|left|150px]] |version2 = [[File:Sigil of woodcraft (attuned) detail.png|left|150px]] }} The '''Sigil of Woodcraft''' is a tier 3 skilling [[Deadman Mode]] sigil. It is a toggleable permanent unlock that gives [[planks]] rather than [[Woodcutting#Logs|logs]] when chopping trees. [[Coins]] are required, and the effect does not work in [[Deadman Mode#Town protection|guarded areas]] or with the [[infernal axe]].
It is a toggleable unlock and can be toggled on and off through the "Unlocks" option on the [[deadman's skull]].
In [[Deadman: Annihilation]], it can be purchased from the [[Deadman: Annihilation/Skull shop|skull shop]]. It can be activated by clicking ''Attune'' and is a permanent unlock. There is no limit on how many permanent sigils can be active at once. Duplicate sigils can be sold back to the skull shop by using them on the [[deadman's skull]].
In past [[Deadman Mode]] events, the un-attuned version was dropped by most monsters (via the [[Drop table#Deadman Mode|Deadman Mode drop table]]) and was tradeable on the [[Grand Exchange]].
==Effect== {|class=wikitable !Event !Effect |- class="table-yes" |[[Deadman: Annihilation]] |Instead of receiving [[Woodcutting#Logs|logs]] when chopping specific [[Woodcutting#Types of trees|trees]], you will receive the appropriate [[planks]]. Requires 50 coins per [[regular plank]], 125 coins per [[oak plank]], 250 coins per [[teak plank]], and 700 coins per [[mahogany plank]]. Does not work in [[Deadman Mode#Town protection|guarded areas]] or with the [[infernal axe]]. |- |[[Deadman: Armageddon]] |Instead of receiving logs when chopping specific trees, you will receive the appropriate planks. Does not work in guarded areas or with the infernal axe. |- |[[Deadman: Apocalypse]] |Instead of receiving logs when chopping specific trees, you will receive the appropriate planks. Does not work in guarded areas or with the infernal axe. |}
The cost per plank is as follows: {| class="wikitable" |- !colspan=2|Item !Cost |- |{{plinkt|Plank}} |{{coins|50}} |- |{{plinkt|Oak plank}} |{{coins|125}} |- |{{plinkt|Teak plank}} |{{coins|250}} |- |{{plinkt|Mahogany plank}} |{{coins|700}} |}
