{{Infobox Scenery |version1 = Land's End |version2 = Southern Expanse |name = Sign |image1 = [[File:Sign (Sea charting, Land's End).png|150px]] |image2 = [[File:Sign (Sea charting).png|220px]] |release = [[19 November]] [[2025]] |update = Sailing is OUT TODAY! |members = Yes |quest = No |location1 = [[Great Sound]] |location2 = [[Southern Expanse]] |options = Chart |examine1 = The Kourend tourist board may have gone too far this time. |examine2 = Welcome to nowhere. Please sail carefully. |map1 = {{Map|name=Sign|1529,3405|mtype=pin}} |map2 = {{Map|name=Sign|1828,2138|mtype=pin}} |id1 = 59366 |id2 = 59365 }} '''Signs''' are [[sea charting]] objects found on a small island south-east of [[Land's End]] and south of the [[Isle of Serpents]].
Upon charting the sign in the [[Great Sound]], a game message appears stating {{mes|The sign informs you that this is where the sea begins. You note it down in case it isn't a joke.}}
Meanwhile, charting the glider in the [[Southern Expanse]] results in a game message stating {{mes|The sign proudly states that there is nothing south of here, so you note that down.}}
